# 23. Event Evidence Levels

Event evidence should be classified into three levels.

## Level 1 — Architectural

Proves that the event concept exists in the architecture.

```text
Status:
ARCHITECTURALLY IDENTIFIED
```

## Level 2 — Runtime Observed

Proves that the event was actually produced or observed by the runtime.

```text
Status:
OBSERVED
```

## Level 3 — Certified

Proves that the event conforms to the approved contract and participates correctly in trace, validation, and replay.

```text
Status:
CERTIFIED
```

These levels must not be conflated.

